As section 4(b) of the Apache License requires, a statement of changes:
these files were modified from the originals by being translated to Rust.
The translation keeps the original file layout (one Rust module per C++
source file), function order, comments and error messages; C++ exceptions
became Rust `Result` errors, and additional checks return errors where
the C++ code would read out of bounds or recurse without limit on
malformed input. Each translated file says, in its header, which original
files it translates and that it is an altered version.

SPIRV-Cross itself carries no NOTICE file.

src/spirv_cross/spirv.rs is generated (by tools/gen_spirv_headers.py)
